## Quick Checklist

1. ✅ Set up framework + styling
2. ✅ Wireframe + component library
3. ✅ Build core UI components
4. ✅ Implement state management
5. ✅ Connect to backend APIs
6. ✅ Add routing & dynamic pages
7. ✅ Optimize images & bundles
8. ✅ Write unit & E2E tests
9. ✅ Deploy & monitor

---

### Final Thought

Building a robust e‑commerce front‑end is all about modularity, performance, and a smooth user journey. Start small—get a single page working end‑to‑end—then iterate. Keep your codebase clean, test often, and let the community’s tooling (Next.js, Nuxt, Tailwind, Jest, Cypress) do the heavy lifting.

Happy coding! 🚀
